# composeApp Architecture

Source of truth: `composeApp/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Dependency direction (top → bottom only)

`ui` → `MainStateHolder` → (`base` | `helper` | `net`) → device/OS  
`data` / `utils`: no Compose UI, no ADB, no process execution.

## Must

- New features: state/use-case in `MainStateHolder`; pages only bind UI
- Routes only via `data/Constants.kt` `mainItemMap`
- New deps via `gradle/libs.versions.toml` + `libs.*`
- AYA protocol changes: sync desktop bean/helper with `server/`

## Must not

- UI calling `AdbClient` / `PlatformAdapter` directly
- Second DI or HTTP stack replacing Koin / Ktor
- Merging `server/` into composeApp
- Weakening single-instance lock or undecorated window without explicit request
